    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count the students who made mistakes",
        "body": "$10\\%$ got question 1 wrong, $20\\%$ got question 2 wrong and $30\\%$ got question 3 wrong. The number of students who got at least one question wrong is as large as possible when these groups do not overlap, and then it is $10\\%+20\\%+30\\%=60\\%$. So at least $100\\%-60\\%=40\\%$ got everything right.\n\nThis is achievable: let the students who fail question 1, 2, 3 be three separate groups of $10\\%$, $20\\%$, $30\\%$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 40%**"
      }
