      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "84"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "112"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Count the routes step by step",
        "body": "Label the grid with B in the top-left corner, A, N in the first row, then A, N, A, then N, A, N. For each letter, write in each cell the number of ways to read the word so far ending in that cell; each cell's number is the sum of the numbers of the neighbouring cells from the previous step.\n\n- B: 1 (the top-left cell).\n- BA: the two cells next to B get 1 each.\n- BAN: top-right N gets 1, the centre N gets 2, the bottom-left N gets 1.\n- BANA: each of the four A cells gets 3.\n- BANAN: top-right N 6, centre N 12, bottom-left N 6, bottom-right N 6.\n- BANANA: the A cells get $18,\\ 18,\\ 24,\\ 24$.\n\nTotal: $18+18+24+24=84$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 84**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Count by the position of the first N",
        "body": "The first N can be top-right, centre or bottom-left (the bottom-right N cannot be reached by the second letter). If the first N is top-right (or by symmetry bottom-left), the word then returns to an A and goes on to a second N and an A, which gives $14$ readings each. If the first N is in the centre, there are $56$ readings. Total: $14+14+56=84$.\n\n**Answer: (D) 84**"
      }
    ],
